{"id":90741162,"slug":"31-of-those-suffering-with-treatment","title":"31% Of People With OCD Could Be In Remission","subtitle":"... if they were given access to an FDA-approved treatment. ","post_date":"2022-12-16T15:35:17.310Z","audience":"everyone","type":"newsletter","canonical_url":"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/31-of-those-suffering-with-treatment","wordcount":445,"source":"api","fetched_at":"2026-09-13T22:00:59.028Z","body_sha256":"7639196d6cd5e0fea9ec46887368f1b10e1239cda6d0ba7b74a0e130b67bc1a3","text_words":777,"complete":true,"body_html":"<p>I have previously published articles on <a href=\"https://open.substack.com/pub/thefrontierpsychiatrists/p/new-hope-for-ocd-is-insurance-covered?utm_source=direct&amp;r=1ct8f&amp;utm_campaign=post&amp;utm_medium=web\">transcranial magnetic stimulation</a> (TMS) and <a href=\"https://open.substack.com/pub/thefrontierpsychiatrists/p/i-dont-have-ocd-i-just-obsess-constantly?utm_source=direct&amp;r=1ct8f&amp;utm_campaign=post&amp;utm_medium=web\">obsessive compulsive disorder</a>. Obsessive compulsive disorder (OCD) is common, disabling, <a href=\"https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/bjpsych-open/article/resolving-the-discrepancies-of-suicide-risk-in-obsessivecompulsive-patients-a-review-of-incidence-rates-and-risk-factors-of-suicide-and-suicide-attempts-in-ocd/B07F6BA120B93572B83C3C8B5A744120\">10 times more lethal than depression in terms of completed suicide risk</a>, and responds poorly to traditional treatment for 2% of the population. </p><p>Definitions that matter:</p><p><strong>Response</strong>: 50% reduction in symptoms (may still be very sick)</p><p><strong>Remission</strong>: Symptoms no longer present or so mild they don’t qualify as “disordered.” </p><p>Remission is better than response. Remission is what we want from illnesses. Response is what we settle for.  But when we talk about evidence-based treatments, we need to ask the question about what the evidence demonstrated the treatment was capable of doing to help.   Was remission the outcome? Or was it just response?   Now onto the rest of the argument, reviewing recent data about my favorite OCD treatment.  </p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2XxV!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fdcce5e6d-c22f-4af8-8c15-b0e7021756cb_1200x1200.jpeg\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2XxV!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fdcce5e6d-c22f-4af8-8c15-b0e7021756cb_1200x1200.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2XxV!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fdcce5e6d-c22f-4af8-8c15-b0e7021756cb_1200x1200.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2XxV!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fdcce5e6d-c22f-4af8-8c15-b0e7021756cb_1200x1200.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2XxV!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fdcce5e6d-c22f-4af8-8c15-b0e7021756cb_1200x1200.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2XxV!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fdcce5e6d-c22f-4af8-8c15-b0e7021756cb_1200x1200.jpeg\" width=\"1200\" height=\"1200\" data-attrs=